& [Delineation]
  + Slice11 owns governed fixture artifacts an experiment-only MCP client bridge transcript construction measurement and result preservation
  + Slice7 remains lifecycle judgment owner Slice8 remains stateless transport owner Slice9 remains immutable custody owner and Slice10 remains volatile custody transport owner
  + llama.cpp remains an unmodified provider reached only through its existing OpenAI-compatible HTTP surface
  + model-visible calls carry selection or compact lookup input and never proof-bearing signatures receipts or trust facts invented by the model

& [DualHemisphereReview]
  + [expansive] a live two-checkpoint experiment makes Cantor observable as an inference coprocessor rather than only a protocol library
  + [analytic] checked-in canonical request bytes avoid dependency cycles production fixture machinery and uncontrolled model-authored evidence
  + [reconciliation] host-owned fixture selection and registration combine with one model-authored bounded tool call while exact core response equality remains machine-verified outside model prose

& [DataDesign]
  + canonical JSON request bytes are source fixture data
  + fixture SOP manifests expected response digests transcripts and measurement summaries are distinct provenance-bearing records
  + token counts latency and byte counts are observations rather than semantic authority
  + the volatile handle is a locator into one process and never a durable key credential or reconstructed meaning

& [FeatureRequirementSupport]
  + governed valid and lifecycle-refused fixtures are the first dependency
  + a shared experiment-only MCP subprocess client is the second dependency
  + the existing checkpoint transcript seam is ready and depends only on replacing the local reflect boundary
  + a live pinned provider is an environmental dependency and cannot block provider-independent implementation or tests

& [SecurityAndHonesty]
  + the experiment exposes no build filesystem signing admission installation deployment or general process authority to the model
  + fixture signing keys are deterministic test identities only and are never accepted as production trust roots
  + exact typed response equality is checked by the host and is not delegated to model judgment
  + unavailable provider state must remain an explicit unrun frontier

& [ModelRouting]
  + [suitability] requires_deeper_reasoning_for_SJS_and_cross_system_bridge_design
  + bounded fixture generation unit tests lint repairs evidence refresh and proof updates become Spark-suitable only after phase lock
  + no sub-agent or model switch is activated in this conversation

& [Decision]
  + [status] accepted_for_canonicalization_and_phase_lock
  + [fixture_shape] two checked-in compact canonical JSON lifecycle requests with a signed SOP fixture manifest and snapshot-equivalence tests
  + [bridge_shape] experiment-only Rust harness using official rmcp child-process clients for Slice8 and Slice10 and the existing unmodified llama.cpp checkpoint flow
  + [live_execution_condition] only when a pinned local endpoint is observed healthy and its model identity matches the experiment record
